  "thesis": "The Limit Break AMM's extension points (pool types, transfer handlers, token hooks) are protected by defense-in-depth: pool type outputs bounded by reserve arithmetic, handler transfers validated by balance snapshots, hook fees capped by swap amounts, and reentrancy blocked by the ENTERED bit. The identified reentrancy window during hook fee distribution (EH-001) is a defense-in-depth concern but not exploitable for value extraction due to CEI pattern. Pool type trust (EH-002) is by-design. No exploitable vulnerability found that enables an attacker to extract value across trust boundaries."
